    Modifying the code to allocate more memory than available could lead to allocation failure.

    ```cpp
    char* ptr = nullptr;
    allocateMemory(&ptr, SIZE * SIZE * SIZE * SIZE); // Attempt to allocate excessive memory
    // If allocation fails, an error message will be printed, but no crash occurs.

    conditionalFree(&ptr, 1);
    // Gracefully handles if `ptr` is nullptr.

    freeMemory(&ptr);
    // Also gracefully handles if `ptr` is nullptr.

